        "like": 8
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This has been the case since the IK update. During the beta for that build we found custom walking animations were only updating locally. So generic animations or humanoid animations affecting game objects weren't updating for anyone else. There's a another canny that's marked under review for this same issue. https://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/non-humanoid-keyframes-in-custom-movement-animations-not-synced\n\nI share your frustration though, It's yet another feature creators have lost. Final IK broken, walking animations broken, and soon now audio will be limited. Not to mention after nearly 2 years of playing this game there hasn't been any significant updates to the avatar sdk apart from a broken ik follower and avatar stats. If anything they need a better way to monetize the game so they can focus on delivering more content. These days I can't tell if it's utter incompetence or a lack of resources though I assume it's the latter with the fact that this is still a free game.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
